  "architecturalPlan": {
    "scaleRationale": "This targeted revision retains the established expansive waterfront residence rather than inflating its programme. The meaningful change is the completion of the already-modelled upper west suite as a genuine private outdoor room: a compact elevated terrace makes the taller west anchor useful, improves its proportion against the central salon, and avoids adding unjustified new amenities or detached buildings.",
    "arrivalAndCirculation": "Landward arrival remains through the limestone court, framed portal and recessed bronze entrance beneath the dedicated timber canopy. The entrance leads into the tall central salon. The principal oceanward route is now physically resolved by replacing the salon’s central glazed bay with a full-height bronze terrace door, providing direct movement from the salon to the covered ocean terrace, pool court and pavilion. The elevated west-suite terrace is connected to its existing ocean-side upper-suite door; vertical circulation to that upper suite remains unmodelled.",
    "volumeHierarchy": "The composition is preserved as a tall central living salon, a more private low east wing, and a distinct recessed two-storey west anchor. The new upper west terrace extends the upper suite toward the water without enlarging the enclosed mass, strengthening the intended stepped primary-secondary hierarchy. The central salon remains the principal communal volume, with the lateral wings subordinate and the pool pavilion detached beyond the terrace.",
    "relationshipsAndViews": "Three ocean-facing salon bays remain legible, but the centre bay is now an operable threshold rather than an inaccessible glazed opening. The flanking glazed bays retain framed ocean views. The deep covered terrace remains the principal shared outdoor room; new lateral bronze slat screens make its exposed edges more private and reduce lateral glare while preserving the forward outlook. The upper west terrace is enclosed by transparent guards on its exposed edges and retains the existing ocean-facing suite door.",
    "roofFacadeAndMaterials": "The stepped flat-roof composition is retained: the highest limestone salon roof reads as the communal centre, while the smaller upper-west roof remains set back over the suite. Ivory enclosure, limestone floor and roof edges, timber canopies, and selective bronze doors/screens are consolidated into a restrained tropical palette. New bronze terrace screens provide facade depth and shade without turning every elevation into a repetitive glazed grid.",
    "intendedSpaces": [
      "Covered landward arrival court with recessed entrance portal",
      "Tall central salon with operable ocean terrace threshold",
      "West private suite wing with elevated ocean terrace",
      "East private suite and flexible support wing",
      "Deep covered ocean-facing dining and lounge terrace with lateral privacy shade",
      "Rectangular pool court with coping and basin geometry",
      "Detached open elliptical ocean lounge pavilion"
    ],
    "designDecisions": [
      {
        "disposition": "constructed",
        "knowledgeId": "facade-materials",
        "decision": "Reinforced a restrained palette and facade depth through the existing ivory/limestone/timber composition, a bronze salon door, and lateral bronze terrace screens.",
        "elementIds": [
          "salon-view-center",
          "salon-ocean-door",
          "terrace-screen-west",
          "terrace-screen-east",
          "terrace-canopy"
        ],
        "limitation": "No solar, weathering, or material-performance simulation is represented."
      },
      {
        "disposition": "constructed",
        "knowledgeId": "estate-composition",
        "decision": "Retained the central salon as the primary communal volume and made the pre-existing upper west suite a more useful secondary private volume through an actual guarded terrace rather than adding more programme.",
        "elementIds": [
          "salon-floor",
          "west-upper-floor",
          "west-upper-terrace-deck",
          "west-upper-terrace-rail",
          "west-upper-terrace-rail-west",
          "west-upper-terrace-rail-east"
        ],
        "limitation": "Upper-suite internal programme and vertical access are not geometrically modelled."
      },
      {
        "disposition": "constructed",
        "knowledgeId": "roof-main-secondary",
        "decision": "Kept the salon roof dominant and the west upper roof subordinate; the new terrace projects beyond the recessed upper roof as an intentionally open, guarded outdoor room.",
        "elementIds": [
          "salon-roof",
          "west-upper-roof",
          "west-upper-terrace-deck",
          "west-upper-terrace-rail"
        ],
        "limitation": "The open upper terrace is not roof-sheltered; waterproofing, drainage, guard compliance, and engineering are not verified."
      },
      {
